; Two vectors whose shapes cannot be broadcast are fatal on both substrates and
; must fail closed: nonzero exit, a diagnostic on stderr, nothing past the form.
;
; Native used to answer this one SILENTLY AND WRONGLY. The Scheme-vector
; element-wise kernel loops to operand 1's length over BOTH operands' element
; arrays, so the two-element operand was read past its end:
;
;   (* (vector 1 2 3) (vector 4 5))   before  #(4 10 4.4e-323), exit 0
;                                             — the last element is whatever
;                                             followed the vector in the arena
;                                     after   Shape mismatch in tensor-mul:
;                                             shapes (3) and (2) are not
;                                             broadcast-compatible, exit 1
;
; The VM has no vector arithmetic under `*` at all and has always refused the
; whole family loudly, so it was never wrong here — only native was, which is
; why this belongs in the fail-closed ratchet rather than the corpus.
(display (* (vector 1 2 3) (vector 4 5)))
(display "MUST-NOT-PRINT")
